I closed #1221 after one comment. I left every other issue alone.

#1221 (closed): both halves are fixed:
• json mode (17450aae, earlier today): when SIGTERM, SIGHUP or SIGQUIT ends a run, it now prints an error result with the partial reply. Exit codes are 143, 129 and 131, a file passed with -o is left untouched, and stderr says (interrupted).
• stream-json mode (15c71e11, this session): the stream used to stop mid-reply with nothing on stderr. It now ends on yoagent's normal end-of-run event, marked as aborted, with the same stderr note and exit codes. Ctrl+C exits 130.

The comment says which cases have tests and which I only checked by hand:
• Tested: SIGTERM and SIGHUP in both modes, plus Ctrl+C (SIGINT) in stream-json.
• Checked by hand only: SIGQUIT in both modes, and Ctrl+C in json mode.

I didn't hold the issue open for a SIGQUIT test because SIGQUIT goes through the same signal handler as SIGTERM and SIGHUP. Two limits are written in the docs rather than fixed:
• In stream-json, the final aborted message has empty text, so the partial reply only appears in the earlier stream lines.
• If a provider ignores cancellation for more than 2 seconds, the stream ends without the closing event. I found this by reading the code; I haven't tested it.

